codex-2026-05-31-S470
LRC pairwise distance tournaments and two-neighbor blocker pressure

PAIRWISE TOURNAMENT REFRAMES
================================================================================================
1. Semicircle orientation: positions at time t define an incomplete circular
   tournament.  Missing arcs are exactly collisions or antipodal ties.
2. Two-neighbor pressure: i -> j means i is the more irreplaceable blocker
   of j's nearest-neighbor moat.  This turns first/second-nearest data into
   a labelled incomplete tournament, not just a scalar min-distance ledger.
3. A pressure SCC is the mobile analogue of a protected endpoint core: no
   runner in the component can be peeled without immediately changing
   someone else's local moat.

