SYNTHESIS
================================================================================================
The origin-only LRC ledger forgets two pieces of structure:
* whether the tight runner has one blocker or a two-sided pair of blockers;
* whether blocker dependence peels like a DAG or closes into an SCC.

For a proof search, the useful invariant is not just max_i d1(i).
Keep the ordered pair (d1(i), d2(i)) and the deletion relief
  relief_i(j) = nearest_i(after deleting j) - nearest_i.
Those reliefs form an incomplete tournament whose cyclic core can be
compared directly with the old endpoint-protection core.

A concrete n=14 target suggested by this pass:
  Any attempted all-protected endpoint row should induce either
  (a) a pressure leaf, giving a private runner/endpoint to peel, or
  (b) a strict pressure SCC whose labels must satisfy the same kind of
      arithmetic cycle constraint as THM-365's endpoint cycles.

The second-nearest runner distance is the missing datum.  Without it,
deleting a nearest neighbor has no measurable relief, so nearest-neighbor
graphs alone cannot distinguish a rigid two-sided moat from a fragile
one-blocker moat.
